# `@plank/server` path aliases

In `packages/plank-server`, **always use the `@/` alias** for internal imports. Do not use relative `./` or `../` imports to reach other files under `src/`.

`@/*` maps to `./src/*` (see `packages/plank-server/tsconfig.json`).

```ts
// ❌ BAD
import { route } from "../../../server/module";
import { ClientError } from "../../server/errors";
import { EventBusModule } from "../modules/event-bus/event-bus.module";
import { ClientError, ServerError } from "./errors";

// ✅ GOOD
import { route } from "@/server/module";
import { ClientError } from "@/server/errors";
import { EventBusModule } from "@/modules/event-bus/event-bus.module";
import { ClientError, ServerError } from "@/server/errors";
```

When editing existing files, replace relative internal imports with `@/` equivalents.

## Do not

- Path-map workspace packages (e.g. do not add `"@plank/db": [...]` in `paths`) — keep those as package imports (`@plank/db`, `@plank/common`).
- Invent other aliases; only `@/` for server internals.

## Consumers that load server source via tsx

`@plank/client` and `plank-api` resolve `@plank/server` to source. Their tsconfigs must keep `"@/*": ["…/plank-server/src/*"]` so runtime alias resolution works.
